  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0123, and it contains six tables. The first table is Customer, which has five columns: Address, Contact, Gender, ID (primary key), and Name. The second table is Supplier, which has four columns: Address, Contact, ID (primary key), and Name. The third table is Product, which has four columns: Description, ID (primary key), Inventory_Quantity, and Name. The fourth table is Staff, which has four columns: ID (primary key), Name, Phone, and Position. The fifth table is Purchase_from_Supplier, which has eight columns: Operator_ID (foreign key referencing Staff), Product_ID (foreign key referencing Product), Purchase_Product_Unit_Price, Purchase_Quantity, Purchase_Time, Supplier_ID (foreign key referencing Supplier), and a composite primary key consisting of Supplier_ID, Product_ID, and Purchase_Time. The sixth table is Sales_Product, which has eight columns: Customer_ID (foreign key referencing Customer), Operator_ID (foreign key referencing Staff), Product_ID (foreign key referencing Product), Quantity_of_Sales_Product, Sales_Time, Unit_Price_of_Sales_Product, and a composite primary key consisting of Product_ID, Customer_ID, and Sales_Time.",
  "gold_question": "The main function of a commercial sales management system is to manage customer orders, supplier information, product information, and salesperson performance. The tables involved in the system include customers, suppliers, products, staff, and related order and sales records. The core requirements of the system are: Manage customer information: record basic customer information, including contact information, address, etc. Manage supplier information: track the supplier source of the product, and record the supplier's contact information and address. Manage product information: store detailed information about the product, including product name, description, and inventory quantity. Manage staff information: record information about staff related to operations (such as salespersons, buyers, etc.). Order and sales records: track product information purchased from suppliers and sold to customers.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0123.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0123\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supplier` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `purchase_from_supplier` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `purchase_product_unit_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`, `product_id`, `purchase_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_from_supplier_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `supplier` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_from_supplier_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_from_supplier_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_of_sales_product` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price_of_sales_product` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`, `customer_id`, `sales_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_product_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
